This address had a REON account that was deleted.

When an account is deleted here, everything attached to it goes with it, and the
address it used cannot start a new account for {{ months }} months. That window
exists to stop accounts being cycled — deleted and recreated in quick
succession — and it is not a judgement about you or about why you left.

You can register again with this address from {{ until }}.

If you want an account before then, use a different address: nothing stops you,
and nothing from the old account comes back either way — it is gone, not
archived.

We keep no record of the address itself. What decides this is a one-way
fingerprint of it, which can answer "is this address blocked?" and nothing else,
and which is itself deleted once the window ends.

If you did not try to register, you can ignore this message. Someone typed this
address into the sign-up form; nobody gained access to anything.

